div.verse:
1 Pet. i. 13. Wherefore girding up the loins of your minds;  
Psalm ii. 11. serve the Lord with fear, and in truth: laying aside all empty and vain speech, and the error of many;  
1 Pet. i. 21. believing in him that raised up our Lord Jesus Christ from the dead, and hath given him glory and a throne at his right hand.

Abstaining from all  
          Injustice. unrighteousness; 
          Eph. iv. 19. Coloss. iii. 5. 1 Pet. iii. 9. inordinate affection, and love of money; from evil speaking; false witness; not rendering evil for evil, or railing for railing, or striking for striking, or cursing for cursing.

If therefore we pray to the Lord that he would forgive us, we ought also to forgive others; for we are all in the sight of our Lord and God;  
          Matt. xii. 14; Rom. xiv. 10; 2 Cor. v. 10. and must all stand before the judgment seat of Christ; and shall every one give an account  
          For. of himself.

Let us therefore without ceasing hold steadfastly to him who is our hope, and the earnest of our righteousness, even Jesus Christ;  
          1 Pet. ii. 22, 24. Who his own self bare our sins in his own body on the tree: who did no sin, neither was guile found in his mouth. But suffered all for us that we might live  
          In. 1 Pet. iii. 14, &c. through him.
